      "claim": "The term 'fair trade' requires voluntary agency and the absence of structural coercion between economic actors.",
      "evidence": "Standard economic and ethical definitions distinguish fair trade from mere exchange by requiring that parties can freely enter or exit agreements without existential legal or physical penalty.",
