      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Even if 'fairness' is defined solely by contemporary custom, the structural inability of peasants to exit the relationship negates the 'trade' aspect of 'fair trade'.",
      "evidence": "Trade implies a choice between alternatives; serfdom eliminated the alternative of non-participation or participation with a different lord, rendering the exchange non-voluntary regardless of whether specific terms matched local norms.",
